{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790466605,"nonce":"3ka+yFPgQ4lccP2dX0wYyNWsRvc=","message":"2026-09-27: linked mode landed differently from #1's plan (7aa5c0c). No --cfg and no per-plugin entry names: caribou_abi's 'linked' feature makes plugin! emit a static constructor that calls caribou_plugin_register (caribou-runtime) with the plugin's entry. The constructor only installs the host table and records the PluginInfo; caribou_plugin::linked() reads the tables once the runtime is up, since constructors run in no set order. Ash needs no init_calls: wasm-ld runs .init_array entries from __wasm_call_ctors, and the prelink takes the staticlib whole. Next: the driver builds caribou-runtime plus the program's linked plugins as one staticlib per program.","files":null}]}